# Kandelo patch rationale (S24)
#
# Node forbids JavaScript during parts of cleanup and exit diagnostics.
# Checking only bridge entrypoints misses engine reentry paths, so retain the
# engine gate and shared stop state. The bridge installs Node's resident
# fatal handler through a generic callback before contexts are created; the
# engine has no Node logger include or dependency. A returning handler still
# aborts, and the non-Node default aborts without needing a realm or State.
#
# Source-only cleanup; not rebuilt or behavior-qualified. Retention remains
# subject to README.md: Future work: platform omissions.

